Brazilian Portuguese speaker learning US English, A1, finding places in a new home ("Where is the bathroom?", "the bedroom", "upstairs", "next to"). Words with "th" ("the bathroom", "the third floor") keep "th" in their respelling ("BÉTH-rum"), never "f", "d" or "t" ("BÉ-frum" teaches the mistake), and their tips say how to make the sound. Every respelling agrees with its tip. Respellings are readable by a Brazilian (no "rr" for an English "r") and add no vowel the word doesn't have.